In general, for multi-year research projects involving Risk Group materials, a supervisor should tell lab personnel that biosafety approval, training, and risk assessments must be kept current throughout the project—not just at the start. Personnel should be reminded to:

- follow the approved biosafety permit/protocol and SOPs;
- report any changes in materials, procedures, personnel, or risk level before starting the changed work;
- maintain required biosafety training and PPE practices;
- report incidents, exposures, spills, or near misses promptly;
- participate in periodic/annual reviews of the project’s biosafety controls.

